          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em Bousfield-Friedlander model structure
            (
            %a{:href => "#BousfieldFriedlander78"}> Bousfield-Friedlander 78, section 2
            ) is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+spectra"} model structure for spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+sequential+spectra"} model structure on sequential spectra
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+spectra"} sequential spectra
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+topological+sequential+spectra"} model structure on topological sequential spectra
          %p
            As such, the Bousfield-Friedlander model structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presents
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category+of+spectra"} stable (infinity,1)-category of spectra
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            is the classical
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
          %h2#background_on_sequential_spectra Background on sequential spectra
          %h3#sequential_prespectra Sequential pre-spectra
          %p
