          %h2#TheStrictModelStructure The strict model structure on sequential spectra
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structure on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+spectra"} sequential spectra
            which
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presents
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            is the “stable model structure” discussed
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#TheStableModelStructure"} below
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Omega-spectra"} Omega-spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+objects"} spectrum objects
            among the pre-spectrum objects.
          %p
            But for technical purposes it is useful to also be able to speak of a model structure on pre-spectra, which sees their homotopy theory as sequences of simplicial sets equipped with suspension maps, but not their stable structure. This is called the “strict model structure” for sequential spectra. It’s main point is that the stable model structure of interest arises fromit via
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} left Bousfield localization
          #ClassesOfMorphismsOfTheStrictModelStructureOnSequentialSpectra.num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              Say that a homomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_\bullet \colon X_\bullet \to Y_\bullet
              in the category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SeqSpec
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi sSet
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SeqSpec(sSet)
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SequentialSpectra"}
              is
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %strong strict weak equivalence
                  if each component
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi n
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi Y
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_n \colon X_n \to Y_n
                  is a weak equivalence in the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
                  (hence a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
                  of
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realizations"} geometric realizations
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %strong strict fibration
                  if each component
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi n
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi Y
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_n \colon X_n \to Y_n
                  is a fibration in the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
                  (hence a
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"} Kan fibration
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %strong strict cofibration
                  if the simplicial maps
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 0
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi Y
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_0\colon X_0 \to Y_0
                  as well as all
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout+products"} pushout products
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_n
                  with the structure maps of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ∧
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi n
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ∧
                        %msub
                          %mi Y
                          %mi n
                        %mo ⟶
                        %msub
                          %mi Y
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        X_{n+1}\underset{S^1 \wedge X_n}{\coprod} S^1 \wedge Y_n
                        \\longrightarrow
                        Y_{n+1}
                %p
                  are cofibrations of simplicial sets in the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
                  (i.e.:
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphisms"} monomorphisms
                  of simplicial sets);
          #StrictModelStructureOnSequentialPrespectraIsModelCategory.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              The classes of morphisms in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClassesOfMorphismsOfTheStrictModelStructureOnSequentialSpectra"}
              give the structure of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SeqSpec
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi sSet
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi strict
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SeqSpec(sSet)_{strict}
              %strong strict model structure
              on sequential spectra.
            %p Moreover, this is
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+model+category"} proper model category
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
                  with respect to the simplicial enrichment of prop.
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SimplicialEnrichment"}
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#BousfieldFriedlander78"}> Bousfield-Friedlander 78, prop. 2.2
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The representation of
              %a{:href => "sequential%20spectrum#AsDiagramSpectra"} sequential spectra as diagram spectra
              says that the category of sequential spectra is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalently
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor+category"} enriched functor category
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SeqSpec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi StdSpheres
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi sSet
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    SeqSpec(sSet)
                    \\simeq
                    [StdSpheres, sSet^{\ast/}]
            %p
              (
              %a{:href => "sequential+spectrum#SequentialSpectraAsDiagramSpectra"}> this proposition
              ). Accordingly, this carries the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+model+structure+on+enriched+functors"} projective model structure on enriched functors
            %p
              It only remains to check that the cofibrations are as claimed. To that end, consider a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} commuting square
              of sequential spectra
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mo •
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi h
                                  %mo •
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mo •
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo •
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Y
                              %mo •
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mo •
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X_\bullet &amp;\stackrel{h_\bullet}{\longrightarrow}&amp; A_\bullet
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{f_\bullet}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    Y_\bullet &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; B_\bullet
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              By definition, this is equivalently a
              = succeed "-collection" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi h
                                  %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
